# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
dist/
build/

# Calibration bundle model_changes.diff (captured git diff at solve time, large, regenerable)
/results/calibration/*/model_changes.diff

# Per-ISO EIA-860 override CSVs — raw source files (parquet/json) are committed
data/raw/eia-860/*.csv

# PJM energy market offers raw monthly parquets — gitignored because the
# 3-year corpus (2023–2025) is ~3–4 GB compressed.  Re-fetch with:
#   python scripts/fetch_pjm_energy_offers.py
# Then curate with:
#   python scripts/curate_energy_offers.py
data/raw/pjm-energy-offers/

# Derived binned-fleet cache (side output of the fleet loader)
data/raw/_processed-legacy/*.parquet
# The EIA-923 extracts ARE committed: they are small (~16 KB cost,
# ~225 KB generation) and produced once by
# scripts/process_f923_fuel_costs.py; the dispatch fuel resolver and
# the calibration diagnostic read them at runtime.
!data/raw/_processed-legacy/eia923_monthly_fuel_costs.parquet
!data/raw/_processed-legacy/eia923_monthly_generation.parquet
# Derived CAMPD reference artifacts — per-plant parasitic-load factors and
# emission rates, read at runtime by the dispatch LP and calibration report.
!data/raw/_processed-legacy/parasitic_load_factors.parquet
!data/raw/_processed-legacy/plant_emission_rates.parquet
# Per-year EIA-860 plant-level CHP flag lookup (~0.5 MB), produced by
# scripts/build_eia860_chp_by_year.py from the committed EIA-860 release zips.
# The fleet loader reads it so a multi-year backcast buckets each year's gas
# cogens with that year's CHP designation instead of the latest snapshot's.
!data/raw/_processed-legacy/eia860_chp_by_year.parquet

# Generated backcast dashboard data files (frontend/data/backcast/manifest.js,
# benchmark.js, completeness.js) — assembled from the committed registry
# sidecars + bench parts by scripts/build_manifest.py. These ARE committed (so
# a raw checkout's local preview works via the bc-data.js fallback), but only
# the "Deploy site to GitHub Pages" workflow ever refreshes them on main — it is
# the single writer, pushing with GITHUB_TOKEN. Calibration runs still commit
# ONLY their own namespace files (registry/<id>.json, runs/<id>.js, bench parts)
# and must never hand-commit these shared files, which is what keeps concurrent
# sessions merging without conflicts. The root backcast-results.html is a
# static redirect stub to docs/codebase-site/ — committed, never regenerated.

# Codebase-site backcast data subset — generated at deploy time by
# scripts/build_codebase_site_backcast.py from frontend/data/backcast/.
docs/codebase-site/data/backcast/

# Class-totals cache for scripts/derive_offer_curve_jacobian.py (rebuilt on
# demand from the calibration bundles; the CSV it derives IS committed)
data/raw/_processed-legacy/.offer_curve_jacobian_cache.json

